{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2987","id":3140656874,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz8867Mp7q","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2987","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2987.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2987.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2987","number":2987,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"policy: add App Connector support","user":{"login":"matanbaruch","id":36934912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTM0OTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36934912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch","html_url":"https://github.com/matanbaruch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implement App Connector functionality for Headscale, allowing nodes to advertise as app connectors and receive domain-based routing configuration from the control plane. This addresses issue #1651.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Core Implementation\n- Add `appConnectors` field to Policy struct for defining app connector configurations in ACLs\n- Parse app connector configuration including name, connectors (tags or \"*\"), domains (with wildcard support), and optional routes\n- Add validation for app connector configuration (domains, tags, etc.)\n- Add `AppConnectorConfigForNode` method to PolicyManager to get matching configurations for nodes advertising as app connectors\n- Update mapper to add `tailscale.com/app-connectors` capability to CapMap in MapResponse for nodes advertising as app connectors\n\n### Tests\n- Add comprehensive unit tests for app connector functionality (`hscontrol/policy/v2/appconnector_test.go`)\n- Add integration tests (`integration/appconnector_test.go`):\n  - `TestAppConnectorBasic`: Tests tagged nodes receive app connector configuration\n  - `TestAppConnectorNonMatchingTag`: Tests non-matching tags are excluded\n  - `TestAppConnectorWildcardConnector`: Tests wildcard connector matching\n\n### Documentation\n- Add App Connectors section to `docs/ref/acls.md` with configuration examples\n- Add App Connectors to feature list in `docs/about/features.md`\n- Add CHANGELOG.md entry\n\n## Example ACL Configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tagOwners\": {\n    \"tag:connector\": [\"user@example.com\"]\n  },\n  \"appConnectors\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Internal Apps\",\n      \"connectors\": [\"tag:connector\"],\n      \"domains\": [\"internal.example.com\", \"*.corp.example.com\"],\n      \"routes\": [\"10.0.0.0/8\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. Configure tagged nodes as app connectors in your ACL policy\n2. Nodes with the specified tags that advertise themselves as app connectors (`tailscale set --advertise-connector`) will receive the domain configuration\n3. When clients query DNS for the configured domains, traffic is automatically routed through the connector nodes\n\nCloses #1651\n\n<!--\nHeadscale is \"Open Source, acknowledged contribution\", this means that any\ncontribution will have to be discussed with the Maintainers before being submitted.\n\nThis model has been chosen to reduce the risk of burnout by limiting the\nmaintenance overhead of reviewing and validating third-party code.\n\nHeadscale is open to code contributions for bug fixes without discussion.\n\nIf you find mistakes in the documentation, please submit a fix to the documentation.\n-->\n\n<!-- Please tick if the following things apply. You… -->\n\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\n- [x] added unit tests\n- [x] added integration tests\n- [x] updated documentation if needed\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md\n\n<!-- If applicable, please reference the issue using `Fixes #XXX` and add tests to cover your new code. -->","created_at":"2026-01-01T12:34:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T20:10:47Z","closed_at":"2026-03-01T20:09:13Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d3d8a406801394097872895f41d462d7458499fb","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.gi